You can check imsVops with Ue Radio Capability check.(see 38.413 8.14.2	UE Radio Capability Check procedure, and 23.502 4.2.8a	UE Capability Match Request procedure). You need to check IMS Voice Support Indicator in UE Radio Capability Check Response. But let me warn you about something. Some of gNB's does not support this message yet ( because they don't support voice services completely) so  registration will fail if this procedure not supported by gNB. You can add a flag in your property for disabling this procedure  for working with all gNB's. But at the end  every gNB should support this procedure.

